Description: FixMyCampus allows student to report maintenance, equipment and facility problems around their college campus.

Problem: Students regularly encounter broken equipment or facilities but may not know who to report them to or whether they have been already reported.

Users: Students, lecturers, maintenance and college administrators.

Features: Issue porting, photo uploads, room/building locations, categories, upvoting existing reports, status tracking and an admin dashboard.

Benefits: Makes problems easier to report and allows students to see whether an issue is being addressed.

Feasibility: Very high, it can be developed using standard accounts, forms, images and database functionality.

Uniqueness: Users can follow an issue through stages as "reported->acknowledged->in progress->resolved" rather than simply sending an email.

Why the team should choose it: It solves a problem directly relevant to college life and provides separate student and admin systems, giving each team member meaningful development work
